From: muhnschein <tan_anemone.0l@icloud.com>
Subject: [PATCH] session setup: record the session flags

The SessionFlags of the SESSION_SETUP reply were only used to decide on
encryption and then dropped. A client that must not accept a session the
server silently mapped to guest (SMB2_SESSION_FLAG_IS_GUEST) or to an
anonymous session (SMB2_SESSION_FLAG_IS_NULL) cannot tell.

Record the flags in the context before the signing checks run and add
smb2_get_session_flags(). Recording them before the checks matters: a
guest session cannot be signed, so with signing required the connect
fails, and the caller can still name the reason.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff -ruN a/include/libsmb2-private.h b/include/libsmb2-private.h
--- a/include/libsmb2-private.h
+++ b/include/libsmb2-private.h
@@ -299,6 +299,8 @@
         uint32_t max_read_size;
         uint32_t max_write_size;
         uint16_t dialect;
+        /* SessionFlags of the last successful SESSION_SETUP reply */
+        uint16_t session_flags;
 
         char error_string[MAX_ERROR_SIZE];
         int nterror;
diff -ruN a/include/smb2/libsmb2.h b/include/smb2/libsmb2.h
--- a/include/smb2/libsmb2.h
+++ b/include/smb2/libsmb2.h
@@ -375,6 +375,14 @@
 uint16_t smb2_get_dialect(struct smb2_context *smb2);
 
 /*
+ * gets the SessionFlags (SMB2_SESSION_FLAG_IS_GUEST, _IS_NULL,
+ * _IS_ENCRYPT_DATA) of the final SESSION_SETUP reply. They are recorded
+ * before signing is checked, so a caller can tell after a failed connect
+ * whether the server mapped the session to guest. 0 before session setup.
+ */
+uint16_t smb2_get_session_flags(struct smb2_context *smb2);
+
+/*
  * Set the security mode for the connection.
  * This is a combination of the flags SMB2_NEGOTIATE_SIGNING_ENABLED
  * and  SMB2_NEGOTIATE_SIGNING_REQUIRED
diff -ruN a/lib/init.c b/lib/init.c
--- a/lib/init.c
+++ b/lib/init.c
@@ -660,6 +660,11 @@
         return smb2->dialect;
 }
 
+uint16_t smb2_get_session_flags(struct smb2_context *smb2)
+{
+        return smb2->session_flags;
+}
+
 void smb2_set_security_mode(struct smb2_context *smb2, uint16_t security_mode)
 {
         smb2->security_mode = security_mode;
diff -ruN a/lib/libsmb2.c b/lib/libsmb2.c
--- a/lib/libsmb2.c
+++ b/lib/libsmb2.c
@@ -795,6 +795,8 @@
                 return;
         }
 
+        smb2->session_flags = rep->session_flags;
+
         if (smb2->seal_requested != SMB2_SEAL_NONE &&
             (rep->session_flags & SMB2_SESSION_FLAG_IS_ENCRYPT_DATA)) {
                 smb2->seal = 1;
diff -ruN a/lib/libsmb2.syms b/lib/libsmb2.syms
--- a/lib/libsmb2.syms
+++ b/lib/libsmb2.syms
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@
 smb2_get_client_guid
 smb2_get_compound_pdu
 smb2_get_dialect
+smb2_get_session_flags
 smb2_get_domain
 smb2_get_error
 smb2_get_fd
